<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 49,851 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 49,851 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 49,851 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 69,736 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Wednesday     Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  11,003	  10,119</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  38,848	  59,617</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours four were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,000	 Bunga Tan Jung     28/8</p>
<p>Gas oil		  30,000	 Yang Song Hu	 28/8</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Oscar Acrux	  30/8</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     22,501	 Canan African	31/8</p>
<p>High speed diesel    73,000	 Chesepeak City	2/9</p>
<p>Containers		     500    Song Shan	     2/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
